From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0340-heap-02-nup-cache-cap.patch

Source: 0340-heap-02-nup-cache-cap.patch
Core patch: tools/eglantine-patches, next free number after 0181 (0182 if it goes in first).

NupDecompressCache keeps up to 512 MiB of decompressed zstd files in the heap, for the whole session,
and nothing gives it back when the pool is short. Ocarina of Time is such a NUP. Proven: EDEN_HEAP_SITE
"7 MiB in 1 blocks: ... 378872 2cfe12" is operator new(uncompressed_size) in NupVfsFile::Read (2cfe12
follows that call in next14's image). That line is in the first report only: later reports list
nothing under 10 MiB, so whether the block stayed is not known. How much the cache held in run 61 is
not known either: the site table was full by then (see heap-01).

EDEN_NUP_CACHE_MIB=<N> (at least 16; unset: 512 as now) sets the cap. A file over half of it goes to
a temporary file in cache/nup, the path a file over 256 MiB takes now, which no console run is known
to have used. Those files are removed once per process when the switch is set, because a crash leaves
them behind and the app restarts by itself.

The log gains "EDEN_NUP_CACHE holds N MiB in F files of C MiB, D files of E MiB dropped so far" at each
32 MiB of a new high and each 256 files dropped, with or without the switch. With a small cap, N stops
at the cap: E is what shows how much more was asked for (a file dropped twice counts twice).

clang -fsyntax-only with Boost 1.90 passes (x86-64 host). Not compiled for the console, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/core/file_sys/nup_container.cpp b/src/core/file_sys/nup_container.cpp
index c0e06de01b..de7ee815f2 100644
--- a/src/core/file_sys/nup_container.cpp
+++ b/src/core/file_sys/nup_container.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cstddef>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <cstring>
 #include <list>
 #include <map>
@@ -361,13 +362,54 @@ bool NupContainer::IsNupFile(const VirtualFile& file) {
     return magic == HeaderMagic;
 }
 
+void NupDecompressCache::ReportHeld() const {
+    LOG_INFO(Loader, "EDEN_NUP_CACHE holds {} MiB in {} files of {} MiB, {} files of {} MiB dropped so far",
+             bytes >> 20, lru.size(), cap >> 20, evicted, evicted_bytes >> 20);
+}
+
+namespace {
+
+// EDEN_NUP_CACHE_MIB=<N>: the cache of decompressed files holds N MiB (at least 16) instead of 512.
+// It is heap memory the console's guest and GPU share: Ocarina of Time is a zstd NUP, and run 61
+// ended with 6 MiB free. A file over half of it goes to a temporary file, as one over 256 MiB
+// does now.
+std::size_t ChosenCacheCap(std::size_t cap) {
+    const char* const chosen = std::getenv("EDEN_NUP_CACHE_MIB");
+    if (chosen == nullptr) {
+        return cap;
+    }
+    const std::size_t mib = static_cast<std::size_t>(std::strtoull(chosen, nullptr, 10));
+    return mib == 0 ? cap : std::max<std::size_t>(mib, 16) << 20;
+}
+
+// A session that crashes leaves its temporary files, and the app starts again by itself: once per
+// process, at the first container, when no temporary file of this process exists yet.
+void RemoveOldSpills(const std::filesystem::path& spill_dir) {
+    static std::once_flag once;
+    std::call_once(once, [&spill_dir] {
+        std::error_code ec;
+        for (std::filesystem::directory_iterator it{spill_dir, ec}, end; !ec && it != end;
+             it.increment(ec)) {
+            if (it->path().extension() == ".tmp") {
+                std::error_code ignored;
+                std::filesystem::remove(it->path(), ignored);
+            }
+        }
+    });
+}
+
+} // Anonymous namespace
+
 NupContainer::NupContainer(VirtualFile file_, std::size_t memory_cache_cap,
                            std::filesystem::path spill_dir_)
     : file(std::move(file_)), cache(std::make_shared<NupDecompressCache>()) {
-    cache->cap = memory_cache_cap;
+    cache->cap = ChosenCacheCap(memory_cache_cap);
     cache->spill_dir = spill_dir_.empty()
                            ? Common::FS::GetEdenPath(Common::FS::EdenPath::CacheDir) / "nup"
                            : std::move(spill_dir_);
+    if (cache->cap != memory_cache_cap) {
+        RemoveOldSpills(cache->spill_dir);
+    }
     if (file == nullptr) {
         return;
     }
